# Street life in the staged economy (Docs/Design/79-a-staged-economy.md, section 10 and Phase 8): beggars, the Restday
# dole, rough sleepers and the hungry, and a keeper's business as the shop's day has gone. Built on Phase 6's facts:
# job=beggar while begging (Marketday and Restday, 8:00-18:00, at the chapel steps, the notice board and before the
# shops), on_dole (the priest's Restday bread this week), homeless, hungry, lifted (living on a player's help), business
# (thriving, steady, failing), with the band (wealth) and class beside them, and the market's Times (world.times).
# Never a price figure. Chains: an opener remembers what it spoke of (`jk`: beg, dole, trade_up, trade_same,
# trade_down) and street.answer replies keyed on it; street.close ends it.

## ================================================================ Beggars' barks (concept=bark, job=beggar)

rule e8s_bk_beg_traveller
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.player_near=yes
cooldown 2h
say You there, traveller! A penny for a hungry wolf? | Kind face, that. Kind enough for a penny? | Bless you before you've given. Saves time.

rule e8s_bk_beg_hard
when concept=bark self.job=beggar world.times=hard|lean
cooldown 3h
say There's more of us on these steps every week. | Hard times for all, and harder down here.

rule e8s_bk_beg_good
when concept=bark self.job=beggar world.times=good|boom
cooldown 3h
say Fat times, they say. Not on these steps. | The town's doing well. Let a little of it fall this way.

rule e8s_bk_beg_hungry
when concept=bark self.job=beggar hungry=yes
priority 1
cooldown 2h
say Not a bite since yesterday. A crust, anyone? | I'd take bread over coin. Truly. | Anything to eat. Anything.

rule e8s_bk_beg_winter
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.season=winter
cooldown 3h
say Paws like ice. A penny for a hot cup? | Winter on the steps. The stone takes the warmth right out of you.

rule e8s_bk_beg_dole
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.day=rest here.time=day
cooldown 6h
say Bread after the service. A penny until then? | I'll queue for the parish bread. But a penny now'd not go amiss.

rule e8s_bk_beg_old
when concept=bark self.job=beggar stage=old
cooldown 4h
say I worked forty years, and here I sit. | I had a trade once. Hands won't hold it now.

rule e8s_bk_beg_upper
when concept=bark self.job=beggar self.class=upper
cooldown 6h
say I dined in the Heights once. Don't laugh. | My father kept a carriage. I keep a bowl.

## A beggar a traveller helped (doc 79, 6.7: the one lifted owes its helper, so pair.owed=a is the speaker in debt, and
## lifted=yes while the help lasts: never a loan's debt)

rule e8s_greet_helped
when concept=player.greet pair.owed=a self.lifted=yes self.wealth=destitute|poor topic.meeting=known|returning
priority 1
say You. You fed my household. I've not forgotten. | It's you! We've eaten this week on what you gave. | There's the one who helped us. I'll pay it back one day.

## ================================================================ Passers-by, of the beggars (talk.day, market or Restday)

rule e8s_beg_seen_rich
when concept=talk.day self.wealth=rich here.day=market|rest here.place=market|street
cooldown 2d
say The steps were thick with beggars this morning. One hardly knows where to look. | I gave a penny to one by the board. One feels one should.
remember pair: jk=beg 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_beg_seen_comfortable
when concept=talk.day self.wealth=comfortable here.day=market|rest here.place=market|street
cooldown 2d
say Did you see them by the chapel? Poor souls. | There's a wolf on the steps I used to buy fish from.
remember pair: jk=beg 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_beg_seen_poor
when concept=talk.day self.wealth=poor here.day=market|rest here.place=market|street
cooldown 2d
say There but for the Bright One, eh? | One bad month and that's me on the steps.
remember pair: jk=beg 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_beg_seen_hard
when concept=talk.day here.day=market|rest here.place=market|street world.times=hard|lean
cooldown 2d
say More beggars than stalls, some days. | Hard times fill the chapel steps.
remember pair: jk=beg 2m
then other: street.answer

## ================================================================ The dole (on_dole=yes)

rule e8s_bk_dole_upper
when concept=bark on_dole=yes self.class=upper
cooldown 1d
say I keep my hood up in the queue. | Nobody from the old days saw me. I hope.

rule e8s_bk_dole_middle
when concept=bark on_dole=yes self.class=middle
cooldown 1d
say It's only till things turn. Only till then. | I stand at the back of the line. Less of a show.

rule e8s_bk_dole_lower
when concept=bark on_dole=yes self.class=lower
cooldown 1d
say Bread's bread. I'll queue for it. | No shame in the line. Shame's for them that let it come to this.

rule e8s_bk_priest_dole
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.day=rest here.time=day
cooldown 4h
say Bread for any household in want, after the service! | No one goes home empty from this door today.

rule e8s_bk_priest_dole_hard
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.day=rest world.times=hard|lean
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say The line grows every Restday, and the Bright One sees it. | We'll bake more if we must. No one will be turned away.

rule e8s_dole_tell_upper
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day on_dole=yes self.class=upper
cooldown 2d
say I took the parish bread on Restday. Don't tell a soul. | The priest was kind. That was the worst of it.
remember pair: jk=dole 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_dole_tell_lower
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day on_dole=yes self.class=lower
cooldown 2d
say Got our loaf on Restday. Kept us going. | We'll be in the line again come Restday, and glad of it.
remember pair: jk=dole 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_dole_tell_parent
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day on_dole=yes self.parent=yes
cooldown 2d
say The priest gave the little ones an extra crust. | The pups don't know it's the parish bread. I don't tell them.
remember pair: jk=dole 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_dole_tell_middle
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day on_dole=yes self.class=middle
cooldown 2d
say I queued behind my old apprentice. Neither of us said a word. | The dole's kept us fed. The pride's another matter.
remember pair: jk=dole 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_dole_seen
when concept=talk.day here.day=rest world.times=hard|lean self.on_dole=no
cooldown 2d
say The dole line went right round the chapel today. | I saw families in the bread line I'd never have thought.
remember pair: jk=dole 2m
then other: street.answer

## ================================================================ Business at the counter (barks)

rule e8s_bk_thriving_rich
when concept=bark business=thriving working=yes self.wealth=rich
cooldown 6h
say Another good day. I'll need more hands at this rate. | Steady custom and a full till. That's a year made.

rule e8s_bk_thriving_poor
when concept=bark business=thriving working=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 6h
say Folk are buying! From me! | If this keeps up I'll put a little by before Restday.

rule e8s_bk_thriving_market
when concept=bark business=thriving working=yes here.day=market
cooldown 6h
say Step up, there's a line! | Patience, friends, patience, I've two paws only!

rule e8s_bk_steady
when concept=bark business=steady working=yes
cooldown 6h
weight 0.7
say Same as ever. Same faces, same orders. | A quiet day, but an honest one.

rule e8s_bk_failing_rich
when concept=bark business=failing working=yes self.wealth=rich
cooldown 6h
say Where has the custom gone? It was here last month. | I shall have words with my buyer. This stock won't move.

rule e8s_bk_failing_poor
when concept=bark business=failing working=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say Please. Anyone. Come and look, at least. | I've not taken a penny since morning. | I'll be on the steps myself, at this rate.

rule e8s_bk_failing_hard
when concept=bark business=failing working=yes world.times=hard|lean
cooldown 8h
say Nobody's buying. Nobody's got it to spend. | Hard times empty every till, mine first.

## ================================================================ Business in talk (talk.work, talk.smalltalk)

rule e8s_trade_up_rich
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say A fine season for the shop. I'm thinking of a second. | The books have never looked better. My steward is unbearable about it.
remember pair: jk=trade_up 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_trade_up_small
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving self.wealth=poor|comfortable
cooldown 2d
say The stall's doing well. I keep waiting for it to stop. | Busier than I've ever been. My paws ache with it.
remember pair: jk=trade_up 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_trade_same
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=steady
cooldown 2d
weight 0.7
say The shop's steady. Nothing to boast of, nothing to fear. | It ticks over. That'll do me.
remember pair: jk=trade_same 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_trade_down_rich
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=failing self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say The shop's had a wretched week. One can absorb it, but still. | My stock sits there. I may have bought too much.
remember pair: jk=trade_down 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_trade_down_poor
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=failing self.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say I've stock I can't shift and a till I can't fill. | If it doesn't turn this week I'll shut the door for good.
remember pair: jk=trade_down 2m
then other: street.answer

rule e8s_trade_down_comfortable
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=failing self.wealth=comfortable
cooldown 2d
say Trade's been thin. We're eating into what we'd put by. | Nobody's coming in. I keep sweeping the same clean floor.
remember pair: jk=trade_down 2m
then other: street.answer

## ================================================================ Rough sleepers and the hungry poor

rule e8s_bk_warm_wall
when concept=bark homeless=yes here.season=winter here.time=night|dusk|dawn
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say The baker's wall stays warm till dawn. That's my bed tonight. | The forge doesn't go cold all night. Thank the Bright One for smiths.

rule e8s_bk_homeless_hungry
when concept=bark homeless=yes hungry=yes
cooldown 6h
say No roof and no supper. Some days are like that. Most days. | Nowhere to go and nothing to eat. Spare anything?

rule e8s_bk_hungry_poor
when concept=bark hungry=yes self.wealth=poor self.homeless=no
cooldown 6h
say There's bread enough for tomorrow, if I don't eat today. | Belly's empty, and the purse is lighter still.

rule e8s_bk_hungry_parent
when concept=bark hungry=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute self.parent=yes
cooldown 8h
say Short again this week. The pups ate first. | The little ones had the last of the bread.

rule e8s_bk_hungry_hard
when concept=bark hungry=yes self.wealth=destitute world.times=hard|lean self.job!=beggar
cooldown 6h
say Nothing in the house. Nothing. | I've walked past the bakery three times. Smelling's free.

## ================================================================ Answers (street.answer), keyed on what was said

rule e8s_ans_beg
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=beg
say Hard to see. | It's a shame on the town, that.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_beg_rich
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=beg self.wealth=rich
say One gives at the service. That should be enough. | Dreadful. Somebody should do something.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_beg_poor
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=beg self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Don't. That's me if this month goes wrong. | Half of them worked the same posts as us.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_beg_warm
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=beg warmth=warm
say I'll take them some soup tonight. | Poor souls. Every one of them was someone's pup.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_dole
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=dole
say No shame in bread. | Better the line than an empty belly.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_dole_rich
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=dole self.wealth=rich
say We give to the chapel every season. I'm glad it goes somewhere. | I hadn't realised. I'm sorry.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_dole_poor
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=dole self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I've stood in that line. I'll stand in it again, likely. | The priest's a good one. Never makes you feel it.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_up
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_up
say Good for you! | Well done. You've earned it.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_up_poor
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_up self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Must be nice. | Need anyone to sweep up? I'm cheap.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_same
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_same
say Steady's no bad thing. | That's all any of us wants.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_down
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_down
say It'll turn. It has to. | I'll come by and buy something. | That's hard. I'm sorry.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_down_warm
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_down warmth=warm
say I'll send my neighbours your way. | Don't you shut that door yet. We'll think of something.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_ans_trade_down_cold
when concept=street.answer pair.mem.jk=trade_down warmth=cold
say That's trade. | Then sell something people want.
then other: street.close

rule e8s_close
when concept=street.close
say Aye. Well. | So it goes. | We'll see.
